From bd1c93e1c34e1da9710914e59f915ede2e67a760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:05:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/33] logging: create log plugins from extension metadata

Add support for processing event extension metadata during
log creation and translating it into plugin requests.

Extension requests are extracted from the _EXTENSIONS
metadata container and resolved through the runtime plugin
service. The service bridges log entry processing with the
plugin framework and is responsible for constructing
runtime plugin instances from the supplied requests.

Constructed plugin instances are attached to and owned by
the created log entry, allowing plugin lifetime management
to follow the existing entry lifecycle.

This change establishes the end-to-end flow from event
extension metadata to runtime log entry extensions while
maintaining a clear separation between log management,
plugin integration, and plugin framework responsibilities.

The implementation serves as an intermediate step toward
native event extension support in lg2 EventInfo.

Change-Id: I3ca7d6fd776104114c5e179d8d551292632043ee
Signed-off-by: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
